    "lawCode": "Add §399-oo, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3331B\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to prohibiting\nany person, firm or corporation from soliciting vehicle warranty\npolicies to owners of motor vehicles\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill prevents companies from dishonestly soliciting vehicle\nwarranty policies. It makes it unlawful for companies to make\ndeceptive solicitations for a motor-vehicle warranty where the\nsolicitor erroneously implies there is a current warranty relationship\nwith the consumer.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the bill amends general business law by adding a new\nsection 399-00 titled Deceptive solicitation of vehicle warranty\npolicies, where it shall be unlawful for any company to directly or\nindirectly represent in any manner, whether written or telemarketing,\na false, deceptive or misleading statement. Further this section also\nallows the attorney general to seek damages of a civil fine of not\nmore than $500 for any company that violates this section of law, and\na fine of not more than $1,000 for a company that knowingly violates\nits provisions. Section 2 is separability Section 3 is the effective\ndate.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThere is currently a practice where companies solicit a consumer for\nautomobile insurance coverage implying that the consumer's current\ncoverage is expiring with that company. This practice is misleading\nand deceptive when the consumer does not have a current policy with\nthe solicitor nor is the consumer's policy expiring. This bill makes\nthis practice illegal and creates civil penalties for engaging in this\npractice.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall become a\nlaw.\n",
